    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "case-context-textbook",
        "moduleId": "case-context",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "教材案例：巴黎地铁新信号系统",
        "markdown": "巴黎地铁的新信号系统把相邻列车的最小间隔从 2 分 30 秒缩短到 2 分钟，单次收益为 30 秒；由此增加的线路容量使巴黎地铁不必再修建一条新线路。系统由 GEC Alsthom 开发，包含 9,000 行经过验证的代码。项目 1982 年立项，1985 年完成原型，1989 年投入运营。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-2af98d1121e7e235ed121771",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000032"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Formal Methods in Software Development",
                "Paris Metro Signalling"
              ],
              "lineStart": 377,
              "lineEnd": 393,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "eb35fd2382b4f3543268ac442fa19619237477d67144c5eb44e61b0e64b192df"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "case-capacity-model",
        "moduleId": "case-context",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "模型补充：30 秒为什么是系统级收益",
        "markdown": "把 30 秒放进运营情境中看，它的价值不在单列车速度，而在整条线路的通过能力：列车间隔每缩短一点，同一时段能开行的列车就更多。教材用“免建一条新线路”标示这一收益，说明信号软件的正确性直接连着运营安全与投资决策。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "case-context-textbook"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hoare-logic-textbook",
        "moduleId": "correctness-and-refinement",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "教材：先用 Hoare logic",
        "markdown": "开发初期，团队用 Hoare logic 做正确性证明，因为它是 1982 年可用的最好技术。Hoare logic 是大多数软件正确性证明方法的基础，但使用起来可能相当复杂；开发者不确定如何在如此大的规模上应用它。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-2af98d1121e7e235ed121771",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000032"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Formal Methods in Software Development",
                "Paris Metro Signalling"
              ],
              "lineStart": 377,
              "lineEnd": 393,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "eb35fd2382b4f3543268ac442fa19619237477d67144c5eb44e61b0e64b192df"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hoare-triple-textbook",
        "moduleId": "correctness-and-refinement",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "formula",
        "title": "教材：Hoare 三元组",
        "markdown": "Hoare logic 讨论形如 $\\{P\\}\\ S\\ \\{Q\\}$ 的断言：若执行 $S$ 前 $P$ 成立，且 $S$ 的执行终止，则执行后 $Q$ 成立。纯形式下，如果 $S$ 不终止，它什么也不说明；可以扩展它同时证明终止性。它不是规格说明语言，而是证明代码性质的方法。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-2af98d1121e7e235ed121771",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000032"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Formal Methods in Software Development",
                "Paris Metro Signalling"
              ],
              "lineStart": 377,
              "lineEnd": 393,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "eb35fd2382b4f3543268ac442fa19619237477d67144c5eb44e61b0e64b192df"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hoare-scale-model",
        "moduleId": "correctness-and-refinement",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "模型补充：大规模证明难在哪里",
        "markdown": "Hoare 三元组针对一段代码 $S$ 给出前后断言。系统变大后，需要把成百上千段局部证明组织起来，还要保证每一层的规格与上一层对得上；局部规则本身并不提供这种结构。案例中的困难正来自规模，而不只是公式本身难写。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "hoare-logic-textbook",
            "hoare-triple-textbook"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b-method-textbook",
        "moduleId": "correctness-and-refinement",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "教材：B method 与重新验证",
        "markdown": "Z 语言的开发者之一 Jean-Raymond Abrial 帮助团队重新规格化并重新验证软件。B method 把过程建模为抽象机器，一个抽象机器可以用另一个来实现，这正好对应系统中的不同抽象层次；它支持自顶向下的精化，把抽象机器逐步实现为更底层的机器。Hoare logic 始于 1969 年，而 B method 在教材写作时仍在发展。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-2af98d1121e7e235ed121771",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000032"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Formal Methods in Software Development",
                "Paris Metro Signalling"
              ],
              "lineStart": 377,
              "lineEnd": 393,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "eb35fd2382b4f3543268ac442fa19619237477d67144c5eb44e61b0e64b192df"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "technique-comparison-model",
        "moduleId": "correctness-and-refinement",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "comparison",
        "title": "模型补充：两种技术的分工",
        "markdown": "| 维度 | Hoare logic | B method |\n|---|---|---|\n| 基本对象 | 一段代码及其前后断言 | 抽象机器及其逐层实现 |\n| 主要用途 | 证明代码满足给定规格 | 通过精化组织从规格到实现的层次 |\n| 在本案例中的角色 | 1982 年的初始选择 | 重新规格化与重新验证的支撑 |\n| 规模问题 | 证明繁多、难以组织 | 用层次结构控制复杂度 |\n\n两者不是互相替代的竞赛，而是回答不同问题的工具：一个聚焦代码性质，一个聚焦抽象层次之间的实现关系。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "hoare-logic-textbook",
            "hoare-triple-textbook",
            "b-method-textbook"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "validation-stages-textbook",
        "moduleId": "validation-process",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "procedure",
        "title": "教材：四阶段验证",
        "markdown": "验证被分为四个阶段：需求验证；验证与测试；运行与维护；认证。团队还使用 SADT（Structured Analysis and Design Technique）等工具，并用故障树分析（fault-tree analysis）开展危险性研究。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-2af98d1121e7e235ed121771",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000032"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Formal Methods in Software Development",
                "Paris Metro Signalling"
              ],
              "lineStart": 377,
              "lineEnd": 393,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "eb35fd2382b4f3543268ac442fa19619237477d67144c5eb44e61b0e64b192df"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "proof-testing-textbook",
        "moduleId": "validation-process",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "教材：测试不可被证明替代",
        "markdown": "团队进行了大量测试，并在规格说明中发现了许多问题。教材由此强调两者的分工：测试是弄清程序是否满足真实世界需求的唯一途径；而正确性证明只能说明程序满足它的规格说明。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-2af98d1121e7e235ed121771",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000032"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
